## 3. Each landing module in exactly its own import closure

`python3 -I <OUT>/scripts/gate.py cut …` writes one check file per part and one per patched
existing file: the imports of the target and of the parts in its import closure, the standard
options, the bodies of those parts in file order, then the target's own body. The closure is
computed over the worktree's import graph, so an appended part is included wherever its module
is imported, directly or not. Part K (a replacement) is never included in another target.
```
unit imports: 14; union of the parts' existing imports: 14; missing from unit: []; extra in unit: []
